  "body": "### What happened\n\nIn the Machines pane's file editor, a spindle whose min speed is above its max speed is refused. The refusal shows under all three fields of the \"Spindle range\" group: Spindle min speed, Spindle max speed and Spindle power. I expected it only under the two speed fields. Spindle power has nothing to do with it, so the refusal under it is noise.\n\nThe validator keys this refusal `spindle` (`crates/app/src/machine/validate.rs:230`), and `crates/app/src/machine/fields.rs:177` gives every Spindle range field the refusal key `spindle` in addition to its own key. No other refusal uses `spindle`, so the fix can give that key to the two speed fields only.\n\n<img width=\"762\" height=\"270\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7f113379-208f-44dd-ba98-756c44ee3e75\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the Machines pane, pick \"All\", \"mill\", and press \"New blank\".\n2. In \"Spindle range\", type 1000 in Spindle min speed and 24 in Spindle max speed.\n3. The refusal \"spindle: min_speed 1000 must not exceed max_speed 24\" shows under all three fields, Spindle power included.\n\n### camcraft version and OS\n\n0.24.0 (built from upstream/main a8d923108 plus an open branch that does not touch these files), Windows 11\n\n### Screenshots or recording\n\n_No response_",
